\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb105\sa105\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (10r sqq.) {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Commentarius in librum Boethii de consolatione philosophiae}}\plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24   
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  1r oben \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Materia huius libri est miseria in miseriis gemens, super quibus philosophya tam vere quam valide consolans ... Carmen dicitur a carminando quod est lanam vellere ideo scilicet carptim vel carminatim idest sensim pronunciatur ... 
\line \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Zu Carmen I \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Conquestio Boecii de instabilitate fortune. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Interlinear: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Carmina: idest materias delectabiles quasi cantilenas. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  usw. Marginal \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Camene dicuntur muse quasi canene a canendo, per quas sciencia secularis accipitur. Et dicuntur apud veteres dee carminum; hee scilicet muse novem esse dicuntur vel propter novem instrumenta vocis humane idest duo labia ... 
\line \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  100r zu III 9 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  O qui perpetua mundum racione gubernas: Racionem dicit sapienciam dei idest filium dei, per quem omnia creata sunt et gubernantur ... \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \emdash  Auf Einschaltblatt 20a Kommentar. \emdash  Kommentierung anfangs st\u228 \'e4rker, besonders an Abschnittsgrenzen; teilweise nicht oder schwach kommentiert}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;\red204\green238\blue221;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb105\sa105\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  196v\endash 198r {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Vita Boethii}}\plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24   
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb105\sa105\itap0 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Tempore Theodorici regis insignis auctor Boecius claruit, qui virtute sua consul in urbe Roma fuit. Cum vero Theodoricus rex voluisset tyrannidem exercere .. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \emdash  197v \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 ... Duo tamen filii eius in consolatu permanserunt sub regia potestate. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Dann von Peiper abweichend (197v\endash 198r): \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Cumque libros philosophice consolacionis insignis auctor Boetius viginti septem varietatibus carminum respersit ... \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \emdash  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 ... ad ultimum generum eius clarissimum atque catholicum Boecium, quem paulo ad hoc tantum distulerat, impio ense quemadmodum socerum abreavit (!). \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \emdash  Rest der Seite und 198v leer. 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  Ed. R. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Peiper\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Anicii M. S. Boethii philos. consol., Leipzig 1871, S.XXX\endash XXXII Nr.I\endash II.}

