\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb105\sa105\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  85ra\endash 87vb {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Quaestiones morales et naturales}}\plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24   
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (1) 85ra\endash 87rb \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Queritur, utrum materia forma et priuo (?) sint tria principia naturalia. Et arguitur, quod non. Nulla materia est principium generis ... \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \emdash  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 ... quia raciones et diffiniciones istorum sunt diverse, ergo non est unum diffinitive. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Rest der Seite leer.\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24   
\line \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (2) 87va\endash vb \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Queritur, quare homo quanto plus scit, tanto plus dubitat in se ipso. Ad hoc dicitur, quod duplex est causa. Prima est quia quanto aliquis plus scit, tanto eius intellectus est clarior ... \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \emdash  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 ... non est ita bene tenebrosum}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;\red204\green238\blue221;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb105\sa105\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  88ra\endash 92rb {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Compendium in Aristotelis libros Physicorum}}\plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24   
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  In principio libri physicorum, cuius subiectum est corpus mobile simpliciter non contractum, determinat philosophus de principiis corporis mobilis ipsum constituentibus ... \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Nach der Folge der B\u252 \'fccher, mit scholastischer Gliederung ('Dubitatur...'). 
\line Endet mit Buch VIII 92ra \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  In octavo libro physicorum philosophus ponit, quod aliquis motus est eternus et aliquis motor est eternus. Quot (!) motus sit eternus ostendit tali racione ... \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \emdash  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 ... immobile et incorruptibile, nullam penitus habens magnitudinem. Cui sit honor et gloria et imperium per infinita secula seculorum. Amen. Amen. Amen. >Et sic: Iesus Maria: est finis: / Frater Wilhelmus< \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Mit Glossen}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;\red204\green238\blue221;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb105\sa105\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  93ra\endash 96vb {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Waltherus magister}}\plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24 : {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Tractatus de tribus principiis rerum naturalium}}\plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24   
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb105\sa105\itap0 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Sicut fructus est ultimum quod ab arbore exspectatur, sic ultimum quod exspectatur in actibus humanis sive anime est delectacio, ut ait philosophus 10\u176 \'b0 ethicorum ... \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \emdash  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 ... et ideo in talibus est procedere in infinitum etc. >Et est: Ihesus. Maria: sic finis / frater Wilhelmus / Kehersperger< >Explicit tractatus de tribus principiis rerum naturalium reverendi magistri Waltheri, anno domini 1439< \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Rest der Spalte leer. 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Zumkeller\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Nr.53 (sieht in 'Walterus magister' Walter Burley, legt die Schrift als Dubium dem Aegidius Romanus bei; in Salzburg, B XII 4, Nr.5 die 'Quaestio de esse et essentia' des Aegidius). Der Text findet sich auch Salamanca, BU, 1986, f.190\endash 194v unter dem Titel \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs20  Tractatus trium principiorum Galteri\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20   (Inhaltsverzeichnis f.231v); laut \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Beaujouan\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20   von Burley}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;\red204\green238\blue221;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb105\sa105\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  97ra\endash 108va {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Albertus de Orlam\u252 \'fcnde (?)}}\plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24 : {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Summa naturalium I\endash IV}}\plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24   
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb105\sa105\itap0 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Philosophia dividitur in tres partes scilicet in logycam, ethicam et physicam, sive in moralem et naturalem; quarum duarum omissis ad presens de sola physica sive naturali intendimus ... \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \emdash  Der Anfang von Buch II scheint \u252 \'fcbergangen. III 101va \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Postquam dictum est de corpore mobili in generali et incorruptibili dicendum est ... \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  IV 102vb \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Dicto de corpore mobili generabili et corruptibili simplici nunc dicendum est de corpore mobili generabili et corruptibili composito ... \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \emdash  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 ... De galacia dicit Aristotiles quod ignis purus propinquus orbi inflammatus ... recedens ab eo. Et hec dicta sufficiant ad presens de generatis ex vapore qui coniungitur ex lumine solis, lune et aliarum stellarum etc. >Et sic: Ihesus Maria: est finis / frater Wilhelmus / Kehersperger< Explicit liber metherorum (!) scriptus per fratrem Wilhelmum Kehersperger ordinis Carmelitarum et studens theologie tunc temporis in Avinione, et finitus anno domini 1439\u176 \'b0 in die decollacionis Iohannis Baptiste. 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  Siehe \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Kaeppeli\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , SOP, Nr.112. Ch. H. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Lohr\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Medieval Latin Aristotle commentaries. Authors A\endash F, in: Traditio 23 (1967) 345\endash 348 (ohne diese Hs.)}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;\red204\green238\blue221;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb105\sa105\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  108vb\endash 114vb {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Albertus de Orlam\u252 \'fcnde (?)}}\plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24 : {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Summa naturalium V (rec. II)}}\plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24   
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb105\sa105\itap0 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Hic secundum ordinem tractatus dicto de elementatis inanimatis dicendum est de elementatis animatis. Sed quia ... \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \emdash  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 ... Et hec de anima et potenciis eius ad presens dicta sufficiant. Laus sit Ihesu Christo. >Et est: Ihesus Maria: sic finis / Wilhelmus frater / Kehersperger< \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \emdash  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Explicit tractatus de anima Alberti Magni ordinis predicatorum scriptus per me fratrem Wilhelmum Kehersperger ordinis fratrum beatissime dei genitricis Marie de monte Karmeli. Et finitus anno domini 1439\u176 \'b0 in quinta die que erat sabbati infra Octavas nativitatis Marie. >Regrepsrehek< \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (= Kehersperger) 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 115ra\endash rb Prologus in tractatum Petri de Alliaco de anima \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Veterum tradit auctoritas dignum (!) fuisse illud apostoli oraculum: Nosce te ipsum. Nimis igitur errat qui se ipsum ignorat ... Qua propter de anima et de hiis que sunt in ea tractatum hunc brevem ... compillabo (!) ... \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \emdash  Mit Schemata und Listen. Als Teil des folgenden Textes von Petrus de Alliaco auch in Salamanca, BU, 2085, f.27.}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;\red204\green238\blue221;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb105\sa105\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  115va\endash 128vb {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Petrus de Alliaco}}\plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24 : {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Tractatus de anima}}\plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24   
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb105\sa105\itap0 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Quiditatem anime umbratice oppinantes (!) diversa et adversa senserunt, que omnia asserere longum esset ... \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \emdash  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 ... postuloque michi dari veniam de erratis. >Et sic: Ihesus et Maria: est finis / frater Wilhelmus / Kehersperger< Explicit compendium potenciarum et virtutum animarum editum a reverendo magistro Parisiensi Petro Lyaco (!), scriptum per me fratrem Wilhelmum Kehersperger anno domini 1440 tunc temporis studens theologie in Avinione. Deo gracias. 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  Vgl. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Chappuis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Marguerite und Olaf \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Pluta\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Die philosophischen Schriften des Peter von Ailly, in: Freiburger Zs. f. Philosophie u. Theologie 33, 1986, 593\endash 615, hier 596 (mit dieser Hs.). Kritische Ausgabe von Olaf \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Pluta\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Die philosophische Psychologie des Peter von Ailly, Amsterdam 1986 (Bochumer Studien zur Geschichte der Philosophie, 6)}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;\red204\green238\blue221;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb105\sa105\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  129ra\endash 133va {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Quaestio de distinctione formali et reali}}\plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24   
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb105\sa105\itap0 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Circa materiam distinccionum queritur, utrum illa que distinguuntur formaliter distinguantur eciam realiter. Et arguitur quod sic ... \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \emdash  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 ... sed quia formalitates etc., ideo non valet. Et sic de ista questione dicta sufficiant. >Et sic: Ihesus: Maria: est finis / frater Wilhelmus / Kehersperger.< Deo gracias. 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb105\sa105\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  Zur angeblichen Verfasserschaft des Franciscus de Mayronis siehe Heribert \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Rossmann\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Die Quodlibeta und verschiedene Schriften des Franz von Meyronnes, in: Franziskanische Studien 54 (1972) 1\endash 76, hier 71\endash 72 mit Anm.210. Druck: Venedig 1520 (nicht vollst\u228 \'e4ndig). Auch in M\u252 \'fcnchen, UB, 2\u176 \'b0 Cod. ms. 562, f.103r\endash 106r. 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  133vb\endash 134rb Aristoteles (Ps.): Liber de causis (excerpta) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Omnis causa primaria plus est influens super causatum suum quam causa secunda verbalis. Cum ergo removet ... \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \emdash  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 ... secundum quod ostendimus et exposuimus. Omne esse superius aut est superius eternitate ... \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \emdash  134ra \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 ... quoniam est causa temporis. Omnis anima nobilis tres habet operaciones, nam ex operacionibus eius est operacio animalis et ... \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \emdash  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 ... secundum quod narramus et ostendimus. (?)rmia rerum creaturarum est esse, et ante ipse increatum aliud. Quod est quia esse supra sensum ... \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \emdash  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 ... et incidunt bonitates in eis usquequo consecuntur ultimum eorum. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Ausgabe: \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Bardenhewer\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , 1882, 163\endash 191; \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Pattin\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , 1966. \emdash  Vgl. Aristoteles latinus I 94, 196; II 176}

