\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb105\sa105\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  174v\endash 182v {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Auctoritates diversae collectae ex libris diversis}}\plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24   
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  >Auctoritates diverse collecte ex libris diversis< Seneca. Certum est quod morieris sed nescis ubi vel quando; sed si sapiens fueris ubique eam et omni tempore expectabis iuxta consilium horum versuum: Vive deo gratus toti mundi tumulatus Crimine mundatus semper transire paratus \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Walther\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Proverbia 33938, Initia 20722). \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Unde magister Henricus de Hassia \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  [in]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24   querulacione cuiusdam amici mortui: Si istum mors prevenit munus (!) cautum, vos mortem preveniatis, inde factus caucior (!). Augustinus: O si possimus excitare homines ... 
\line \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Zitierte Autoren und Werke u.a. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Augustinus \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (175r), \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Henricus de Hassia \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (176r), \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Boecius \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (176r, 179rv), \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Rosarium \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (176r), \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Tulius \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (178r), \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Seneca \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (178v), \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Bernhardus \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (181r), Ovid (182rv trist. 2, 1, 266\endash 268; rem. am. 807) \emdash  
\line Endet 182v \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Non est prudentis sic propter verbula gentis Perdere vim mentis sed talia tradere ventis \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (vgl. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Werner\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Latein. Sprichw\u246 \'f6rter des M.A., Nr.168; \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Walther\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Proverbia 17699). }

