\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb105\sa105\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  183r\endash 200v {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 De vita quorundam philosophorum et poetarum excerpta}}\plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24   
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Pitagoras apud Grecos primus immortales dixit esse animas ... \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Ferner Zitate \u252 \'fcber \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Dymocritus \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (!), Anaxagoras, Gorgias, Socrates, Tales, Plato, Epicurus, Zenon Stoicus, Plautus poeta, Terentius, Virgilius: 189v \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Tempore quo regnavit Ptholomeus, Dyonisius anno primo Virgilius puer frequentavit scolas Menelai ... \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  190r \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Anno Octaviani Augusti XXV Virgilius moritur. De hoc Virgilio dicuntur multa actitata: In porta Neapolis Campanie dicitur fecisse muscam eneam ..., macellum ..., hortum ..., Salvatio Rome, \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  190v \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Vincencius: Virgilius tres libros tantum creditur edidisse ... \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  190v\endash 193v \u252 \'fcber \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Dyogenes ... \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  193v Exzerpte aus Ps.-Seneca, De moribus; 195v \u252 \'fcber Thales, 196r Solon, 197r Quintilian, 199v Origenes, 200r Effrem, \u246 \'f6fter zitiert nach dem 'Speculum historiale' des Vincentius Bellovacensis}

