\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb105\sa105\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  3r\endash 21v {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Adelardus Bathoniensis}}\plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24 : {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Euclidis Elementa seu Geometria latina cum commentario}}\plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24   
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb105\sa105\itap0 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Punctus est illud cuius non est pars. Linea est longitudo sine latitudine cuius extremitates sunt duo puncta ... \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Anfang des Kommentars \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Ad cognoscendum, utrum in qualibet figura quot angulos rectos, valent omnes anguli illius figure ... \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  8r \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  >Secundus liber< \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  9v \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  >Tertius liber< \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  13v \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  >Liber quartus< \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  15r \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  >Quintus liber< \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  18v \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  >Sextus liber< \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \emdash  Endet (unvollst\u228 \'e4ndig) mit VI 21 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 ... propter quod lineas proporcionales esse necesse est. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \emdash  Zahlreiche Zeichnungen am Rande. Fensterkommentar. 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  Vgl. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Kristeller\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Corpus translationum. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Folkerts\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Menso: Euclid in medieval Europe, Winnipeg u.a., 1989 (Questio de rerum natura, 2), S.57}

